We can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion for sets:
\begin{align*}
A \cup B &= |A| + |B| - |A \cap B|
\end{align*}
We're interested in the number of boxes that contain neither pencils nor pens, so we need to subtract all pencils and pens boxes from this sum.
\begin{align*}
\text{No pencils and no pens boxes} &= |A \cup B| - (|A| + |B| - |A \cap B|) \\
&= (|A| + |B| - |A \cap B|) - |A| - |B| \\
&= \boxed{- |A \cap B|} \\
&= \boxed{-2}
\end{align*}

